{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"§2 full implementation detail (moved out of the description to satisfy the P4 oversize gate; the description keeps a condensed §2). Original: ## §2 — Live-Cloud coordinator lifecycle module (bounded, self-cleaning)\nNEW `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/test_cloud_coordinator_lifecycle.py` (+ `conftest.py`). Against\nlive REB it drives the epic's CREATE route `coordinate_full_create` (create_route.py:171) — composing\n`coordinate_create` (create_coordinator.py:235; create+commit-unknown) with `contain_created`\n(label/property/confirm binding) — for a plan of EXACTLY ONE throwaway ticket, then exercises the fuse via a\nbounded follow-up mutation (below):\n- **Write-bounding (shared-prod safety).** No full `bridge sync`; no legacy-route `--filter-local-ids`\n  (request.py:95 rejects it here). It acts only on the ONE plan handed to it (one create per plan) — NO\n  enumeration, NO write-back — so the only Jira mutations possible are the throwaway issue's create, its\n  containment label/property, and its delete.\n- **create + binding-lifecycle.** `create_execute` issues the physical create via the live Cloud client;\n  `record_key`/`attach_label`/`set_property`/`confirm` bind+contain it; asserts a confirmed containment\n  (`dependents_released`) with `jira` channel + `jira-` local-id provenance.\n- **commit-unknown recovery.** A second call injects an AMBIGUOUS create signal (simulated timeout) so\n  `_resolve_ambiguous` (create_coordinator.py:211) re-observes ONCE and ADOPTS the existing issue instead of\n  duplicating. Its `observe` FIRST waits until the dedup label search reflects the created issue (reusing\n  §1's helper), so adoption is attributable to the dedup path, not lag.\n- **fuse.** After the create, a bounded NON-create mutation plan (one label/summary op on the bound\n  throwaway key) is driven through `batch_dispatch.coordinate_and_fuse([mutation_plan], execute=...)`\n  (batch_dispatch.py:314) — the correct fuse API (runs non-create `coordinator.coordinate` then folds\n  outcomes through `PassFuse`, pass_fuse.py:96). Asserts the returned `CutoverReport` (tallies +\n  fuse_decisions + degraded) reflects that op.\n- **teardown (always) + one label scheme.** ONE env label `${REBAR_PROBE_RUN_LABEL}` (workflow:\n  `rebar-id:cloudprobe-<github.run_id>`; local: `rebar-id:cloudprobe-<uuid>`) is STAMPED on the created\n  issue by `attach_label`. The module deletes the issue by key in a `finally` (mirrors\n  access_check.py:217-224), then sweeps any issue carrying THAT label — the value §3's sweep keys on, so\n  the two cannot diverge; scoped to this run, not the shared `rebar-id:` prefix.\n- Gated by `_live_jira_ready()` + `REBAR_RUN_EXTERNAL=1` + Cloud creds, enrolling in the all-skip canary\n  (`tests/external/conftest.py`) like the DC modules."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787897083215617001,"uuid":"9bf00e7c-ae1a-4786-b774-96b56a21a48b"}